findings.detail:
The new guard examines only references valid in the current catalog, and routing.snapshot() already omits retired operator references. Adding a model whose ID appears in a dormant stored override therefore bypasses validation. The addition persists successfully, but RuntimePolicy validates that override on restart and throws, preventing daemon startup. Reproduced with this exact command:

bun -e '
import {Store} from "./src/db/store.ts";
import {ProviderTracker} from "./src/router/providers.ts";
import {Router} from "./src/router/router.ts";
import {RuntimePolicy} from "./src/router/runtime-policy.ts";
import {RuntimeCatalog} from "./src/router/runtime-catalog.ts";
import {MODELS,PROVIDERS}

The request says to redact gate output once, where runGates builds a check's result, so every consumer gets redacted text from that one place (budget about 30 source lines). The diff adds about 250 net source lines and also calls redactGateData, a JSON round-trip that redacts and VT-strips every string and injects confinementError, in many other places:
- every `json()` response and SSE message in http.ts, including auth, providers, runs and events;
- every artifact served, where JSON artifacts are re-serialized compactly and text artifacts such as diff.patch and report.md are VT-stripped;
- RunContext's constructor, which rewrites the whole RunState and persists it on the next save;
- imple
